WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.584
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Friday, October thirtieth.

2
00:00:04.584 --> 00:00:12.235
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:12.235 --> 00:00:15.573
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:15.573 --> 00:00:16.953
We start in the Black Sea.

5
00:00:16.953 --> 00:00:21.083
Reuters reports a Greek container ship sank after a drone attack off the coast of Bulgaria.

6
00:00:21.083 --> 00:00:26.996
Greece's prime minister has called for a global maritime truce after the sinking.

7
00:00:26.996 --> 00:00:42.447
In Ukraine, the Institute for the Study of War and the Critical Threats Project report Russian forces carried out daytime long range drone and loitering munition strikes across the country yesterday, killing at least nineteen people and injuring at least eighty two.

8
00:00:42.447 --> 00:00:49.675
In Saudi Arabia, Reuters reports the Saudi-led coalition said it intercepted a drone in the Mecca region, and that the Houthis denied launching it.

9
00:00:49.675 --> 00:01:01.882
ACLED reports Houthi attacks are putting Saudi critical infrastructure under growing pressure, with recent strikes threatening airports and strategic facilities beyond the southern provinces.

10
00:01:01.882 --> 00:01:18.152
In northwest Nigeria, the Nigerian newspaper Leadership reports suspected Lakurawa and Mamudawa militants killed a police inspector and eleven civilians in attacks on several villages in the Koko Besse area of Kebbi State, on Monday, October twenty sixth, and Wednesday, October twenty eighth.

11
00:01:18.152 --> 00:01:20.786
TRAC puts the death toll at up to twenty.

12
00:01:20.786 --> 00:01:32.450
In the Democratic Republic of the Congo, the Critical Threats Project reports former president Joseph Kabila has formally joined the M twenty three rebellion, as political leader of a rebranded movement.

13
00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:44.866
Separately, the U.N. humanitarian office says armed clashes near the Plaine Savo displacement site in Ituri province are disrupting water, health and nutrition services for about seventy six thousand people.

14
00:01:44.866 --> 00:01:48.047
And an update on the Pakistan and Afghanistan border.

15
00:01:48.047 --> 00:01:51.649
The Long War Journal reports the border clashes are continuing.

16
00:01:51.649 --> 00:02:05.217
Global Decipher reports fighting flared again yesterday in the Angoor Adda area, and that a heavy exchange of fire began late last night near the Kharlachi border crossing in Kurram district, opposite Afghanistan's Paktia province.

17
00:02:05.217 --> 00:02:09.633
A Pakistani journalist reports no casualties so far in that exchange.

18
00:02:09.633 --> 00:02:11.849
Now a few quick notes by region.

19
00:02:11.849 --> 00:02:12.770
In Europe, the U.S.

20
00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:22.112
State Department says numerous groups have called for protests across France today and tomorrow, and that recent demonstrations involved looting and attacks on police.

21
00:02:22.112 --> 00:02:27.703
Australia's Smartraveller says nationwide protests are also planned in France on November fifth.

22
00:02:27.703 --> 00:02:33.610
Reuters reports Greece has arrested three people over an explosion that killed six people in Athens.

23
00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:40.597
Reuters also reports four people were killed when an Italian helicopter on a European Union mission crashed in Bosnia.

24
00:02:40.597 --> 00:02:50.404
And Smartraveller says the COP thirty one climate conference in Antalya, Turkey, from November ninth to twentieth may bring road closures and movement restrictions.

25
00:02:50.404 --> 00:02:51.798
In Latin America, the U.K.

26
00:02:51.798 --> 00:02:59.666
Foreign Office updated its Colombia advice with information on a temporary deployment of security forces in the city of Cúcuta.

27
00:02:59.666 --> 00:03:07.347
In Asia, Reuters reports North Korea fired missiles and rockets as leader Kim Jong Un urged dominance in drone warfare.

28
00:03:07.347 --> 00:03:17.002
And in cyber, Reuters reports hackers stole six point three billion dollars from the cryptocurrency exchange Binance, in a theft analysts pinned on North Korea.

29
00:03:17.002 --> 00:03:26.118
Radio Free Europe reports Moldova's president convened the country's national security council after a large-scale cyberattack on government information systems.

30
00:03:26.118 --> 00:03:27.576
That's today's brief.

31
00:03:27.576 --> 00:03:35.857
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

32
00:03:35.857 --> 00:03:44.234
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

33
00:03:44.234 --> 00:03:46.362
This brief is digitally narrated.

34
00:03:46.362 --> 00:03:47.338
Questions?

35
00:03:47.338 --> 00:03:50.884
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

36
00:03:50.884 --> 00:03:52.884
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
